  "content": {
    "id": "p16-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "Find positive integers $a<b<c$ for which:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p16-q9-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$$\\frac1a+\\frac1b+\\frac1c=1.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=2,\\ b=3,\\ c=6$.",
          "worked": "Choose $a=2$ and $b=3$. The remaining fraction is\n$$\\begin{align*}1-\\frac12-\\frac13&=\\frac66-\\frac36-\\frac26\\\\1-\\frac12-\\frac13&=\\frac16.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $c=6$, and $2<3<6$. Check:\n$$\\frac12+\\frac13+\\frac16=\\frac36+\\frac26+\\frac16=1.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$$\\frac1a+\\frac1b+\\frac1c$$\nis a maximum, but less than $1$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=2,\\ b=3,\\ c=7$; maximum sum $\\frac{41}{42}$.\n\nWith $a=2$ and $b=3$, the smallest allowable denominator is $c=7$; all other cases give smaller sums.",
          "worked": "If $a=1$, the sum exceeds $1$, so $a\\ge2$.\n\nIf $a\\ge3$, then $b\\ge4$ and $c\\ge5$, giving\n$$\\frac1a+\\frac1b+\\frac1c\\le\\frac13+\\frac14+\\frac15=\\frac{47}{60}.$$\nIf $a=2$ and $b\\ge4$, then $c\\ge5$, giving\n$$\\frac1a+\\frac1b+\\frac1c\\le\\frac12+\\frac14+\\frac15=\\frac{19}{20}.$$\nFor $a=2$ and $b=3$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac12+\\frac13&=\\frac36+\\frac26\\\\\\frac12+\\frac13&=\\frac56.\\end{align*}$$\nTo keep the total below $1$, we need $\\frac1c<\\frac16$, so $c>6$. The largest allowable third fraction is therefore $\\frac17$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac12+\\frac13+\\frac17&=\\frac{21}{42}+\\frac{14}{42}+\\frac6{42}\\\\\\frac12+\\frac13+\\frac17&=\\frac{41}{42}.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $\\frac{47}{60}<\\frac{19}{20}<\\frac{41}{42}<1$, the maximum occurs at $a=2,\\ b=3,\\ c=7$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 116
      }
    ]
  },
